---
import Journey from '../../layouts/Journey.astro';
import Step from '../../components/journey/Step.astro';
import More from '../../components/journey/More.astro';
import Next from '../../components/journey/Next.astro';
import Fact from '../../components/data/Fact.astro';
import Verified from '../../components/data/Verified.astro';
import { url } from '../../lib/nav';
// The stop lengths below are the made-up ones in journey/chapters/jobs.ts (STOP, OPEN_THREAD).
const facts = ['t3code.worktrees', 't3code.shortcuts.workspace', 't3code.shortcuts.background', 't3code.limited', 't3code.queueSteer'];
---
<Journey chapter="jobs" first="one" title="Several jobs" description="Running several agent jobs at once, in one project or in different ones, with one of you to answer them.">
  <Step id="one" title="While it works, you wait">
    <p>Each job is the agent loop from <a href={url('journey/loop/')}>step 2</a>, run over a made-up hour: your pawn stands by until the job’s lamp turns blue, which means it needs you.</p>
    <p>In <a href={url('journey/parallel/')}>step 7</a> several agents split one task. Here each job is its own, and what runs short is your attention.</p>
  </Step>
  <Step id="three" title="Start another">
    <p>Your pawn walks to whichever job has a blue lamp and stays for a stop; the board holds one card per job. Three jobs keep you busy where one left you standing.</p>
    <More title="Three at once in T3 Code">
      <ol>
        <li>One thread per job. <Fact id="t3code.shortcuts.workspace" /> opens the workspace menu: pick a new worktree, so the job gets its own copy and branch.</li>
        <li>Send the brief with <Fact id="t3code.shortcuts.background" />: the thread runs in the background and a fresh composer opens for the next job.</li>
        <li>Each thread has a diff per turn and its own commit, push and pull request buttons. Merge into main one job at a time.</li>
      </ol>
    </More>
  </Step>
  <Step id="many" title="There is still one of you">
    <p>With five jobs the lamps turn blue faster than your pawn gets round. A bare “Done.” costs 8 made-up minutes a stop, because you read the work to know; proof and a short question cost 2.</p>
    <div class="controls">
      <label class="control"><span>Jobs at once <output>5</output></span>
        <input type="range" min="1" max="5" step="1" value="5" data-bind="n" />
      </label>
    </div>
    <div class="pick" aria-label="What reaches you">
      <button type="button" data-do="stop" data-val="long" data-default aria-pressed="true">“Done.”</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="stop" data-val="short" aria-pressed="false">Proof and short questions</button>
    </div>
  </Step>
  <Step id="projects" title="One project or several">
    <p>In one project each finished job travels the bus to main, one at a time. With several, each job has a small project and an instruction file of its own.</p>
    <div class="pick">
      <button type="button" data-do="projects" data-val="one" data-default aria-pressed="true">One project</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="projects" data-val="many" aria-pressed="false">Several</button>
    </div>
  </Step>
  <Step id="board" title="Keep the board short">
    <p>The label over each job is its card on the board. A card that says “fix” makes you open the thread at every stop, 3 made-up minutes more; a name, a state and what it needs does not.</p>
    <div class="pick" aria-label="How a card reads">
      <button type="button" data-do="board" data-val="vague" data-default aria-pressed="true">A thread called “fix”</button>
      <button type="button" data-do="board" data-val="clear" aria-pressed="false">A name, a state, what it needs</button>
    </div>
    <More title="In T3 Code">
      <p><Fact id="t3code.queueSteer" show="claim" /></p>
      <p><Fact id="t3code.limited" show="claim" /></p>
    </More>
    <Next from="jobs" more={[{ href: 'wiki/parallel-work/', text: 'Parallel work', side: true }, { href: 'wiki/worktree/', text: 'Worktrees', side: true }]} />
  </Step>
  <Verified slot="foot" ids={facts} />
</Journey>
